WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.477
Power isn't only force.

2
00:00:02.477 --> 00:00:04.269
Sometimes it's the ideas we

3
00:00:04.269 --> 00:00:05.795
never question.

4
00:00:06.141 --> 00:00:08.198
Weber described three kinds of

5
00:00:08.198 --> 00:00:09.889
legitimate authority.

6
00:00:09.889 --> 00:00:11.581
Traditional, charismatic,

7
00:00:11.581 --> 00:00:13.187
and legal-rational.

8
00:00:13.552 --> 00:00:15.813
Gramsci called it hegemony.

9
00:00:15.813 --> 00:00:17.554
A class rules by consent,

10
00:00:17.554 --> 00:00:19.033
when its ideas come to

11
00:00:19.033 --> 00:00:21.054
feel like common sense.

12
00:00:21.734 --> 00:00:23.553
Steven Lukes added three faces

13
00:00:23.553 --> 00:00:25.480
of power: who wins decisions,

14
00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:27.150
who sets the agenda,

15
00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:28.594
and who shapes what people

16
00:00:28.594 --> 00:00:30.466
want in the first place.

17
00:00:30.792 --> 00:00:32.063
Your turn.

18
00:00:32.063 --> 00:00:34.897
Hegemony rules mainly through what?
